(FMT-17 — `{var:04x}` is width-4 zero-padded lowercase hex. Hand-verified
 detail the table does not spell out: the width counts the DIGITS, not the
 whole rendering — `{n:04x}` on 255 is `0x00ff`, six characters, because
 the `0x` prefix sits outside the padded field.
 The manual's own row: `{n:04x}` -> `0x00ff`, with n = 255.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox probe.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   0x00ff
)
a number called n is 255.
Print "{n:04x}".
